\f1\fs22 Eloise allowed Hayley to go to the city under stringent conditions.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One: she would travel there, back, and about only by Shakti Enterprises hover-copts and chauffeured ground cars.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Two: She would be attended at all times by a detail, any of whom would be terminated if they failed to keep Hayley always under surveillance and safe.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Three: She would not attempt to contact any of her colleagues at the police department.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley appreciated the first condition, laughed at the third, and asked Sarah for intel on the second.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, those dentist assassins in her entourage? They\'92re definitely expendable,\'92 Sarah confirmed. \'91Please try not to get any of them killed.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley solemnly promised and, as the fan noise of the hover-copt on the Sublime Point pad drowned out their voices, she kissed Sarah goodbye, then stood awkwardly in front of Kathy until Sarah almost pushed her off her feet and Kathy had to catch her. They had a moment, until Hayley regained her composure, straightened, and did that safety dance-step-crouch everyone performs as they approach a full-throated hover-copt.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Excuse me.\'92 Hayley approached the great limping bear of a man, who turned and seemed to be working something out behind his eyes. After a second or so, he\'92d correctly assessed Hayley to be police, and said, \'91What can I do for you?\'92 with a weary tone that suggested he wanted to do nothing for Hayley at all.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Stasis Anomalies Investigator Stockwell?\'92 Hayley asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What of it?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley nodded as if the man had confirmed his identity. \'91May I call you Chip?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip huffed. \'91You\'92d better be getting to the point, Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Okay, so he already knew who she was, but Hayley wasn\'92t unsettled. \'91I believe you made a call on a family recently.\'92 Hayley checked the notes on her tablet. \'91The Chuglinghams?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The Chuglinghams \'85 the Chuglinghams \'85 I don\'92t recall that name.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well that\'92s strange. Records have it you attended their residence for a maintenance call?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Stasis Anomalies Investigators don\'92t do maintenance calls.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well that\'92s what I thought too,\'92 Hayley said innocently. \'91Yet, here\'92s the call-out log from your office on that day. It says, 
\f2\i Stockwell, C.: maintenance call
\f1\i0 .
\f2\i  
\f1\i0 And see here? It says 
\f2\i RESIDENT: Chuglingham
\f1\i0 .\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip tried to grab Hayley\'92s tablet; she deftly evaded his clutch. Chip straightened. \'91Fridge Force does not comment on in-kitchen matters,\'92 he recited from the FF public relations play-book.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Of course. Look, I\'92m not interested in the Chuglinghams,\'92 she said, which was false. The next bit would be tricky. \'91I have information \'85 about national security \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip cast Hayley in his ominous bear-sized shadow. \'91Even a police detective is required to divulge all she knows about stasis security.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes, of course. Are you aware a neighbour of the Chuglingham\'92s\'97one Travis Teh\'97apparently committed suicide while they were away on holidays?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91So?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What if it wasn\'92t suicide?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Murder?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley nodded. \'91That\'92s the line of enquiry I\'92m following.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chip\'92s eyes darted around in their sockets. Hayley smiled to see she\'92d got him thinking.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What if,\'92 Hayley pressed, \'91Mr Teh was murdered in connection with a \'85 violation of the 
\f2\i Refrigeration Secrets Act
\f1\i0 ?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Murder investigations are beyond our purview. Fridge Force does not comment on\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\'97in-kitchen matters, yes, I know.\'92 Hayley chewed her bottom lip. \'91There are some things I don\'92t need you to comment on.\'92 She waited for Chip to comment, but he just rocked on his feet, which she imagined must be compromising the structural integrities of his work boots. \'91I don\'92t need you to comment on whether anyone knows where the Chuglinghams are. It seems they sold up shortly after their arrival home from holidays and \'85 disappeared. Their children were exfiltrated from school around the same time a certain Stasis Anomalies Investigator showed up on the front door of their home, allegedly performing a routine maintenance call.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Fridge Force does not comment\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\'97and I certainly don\'92t need you to comment on whether Travis Teh\'92s murderer \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>But Stasis Anomalies Investigator Chip Stockwell was waddling away. \'91Good day, Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning,\'92 he called back. \'91You\'92ll be hearing from us.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I certainly hope so!\'92 she called in return.
